# Agent Safety Rules

- Do not rewrite unrelated code.
- Do not change scientific logic unless explicitly requested.
- Do not touch large or risky files casually; require explicit permission for high-impact files.
- Do not delete files unless explicitly requested.
- Do not mix refactor and feature work in the same task.
- Do not make assumptions about physics, units, calibration, or timing semantics.
- Stop and report uncertainty when requirements or scientific meaning are unclear.
- Do not create documentation sprawl. Prefer updating existing task documents.
